jobs.description:
The goal is a lightweight iOS app with a clean, minimal interface that performs three core actions:

1. ingest one or more reference images, analyse them, and generate a reproducible mapping table;
2. accept a .txt file (or a .zip that contains one), apply the mapping, then run the data through an encryption layer;
3. save or share the resulting encrypted .txt file back to local storage / Files.

I’m fine with Swift, Objective-C, or any cross-compiled framework as long as the final build runs smoothly on current iPhone models. For encryption I’m open-minded—AES, RSA, or a small custom algorith
